shnabm","html_url":"https://github.com/krishnabm","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/krishnabm/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/krishnabm/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/krishnabm/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/krishnabm/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/krishnabm/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/krishnabm/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/krishnabm/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/krishnabm/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/krishnabm/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-06-24T17:05:52Z","updated_at":"2025-06-24T17:06:13Z","body":"> It's not a good idea to make a whole new line for this. The sentence should be merged with the first line.\r\n> \r\n> Although, since this is common information, it may be worth mentioning it once and for all in the leading description.\r\n\r\nDone. I couldn't find a suitable reference for adding this in the leading description of the method definitions. Let me know if this would make sense somewhere specific and I can include the following line in the description -\r\n`All store_* methods return a boolean value indicating success of the operation.`\r\n\r\nOn the other hand, I feel it would be consistent to return the `Error` enum similar to other set_ and get_ methods. Is this something that can be added to the issue tracker? Also will it break backward compatibility?","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3001235672/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3001403294","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/107938#issuecomment-3001403294","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/107938","id":3001403294,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6y5cee","user":{"login":"Mickeon","id":66727710,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY2NzI3NzEw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/66727710?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mickeon","html_url":"https://github.com/Mickeon","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mickeon/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mickeon/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mickeon/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mickeon/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mickeon/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mickeon/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mickeon/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mickeon/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mickeon/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-06-24T17:58:01Z","updated_at":"2025-06-24T17:58:01Z","body":"> On the other hand, I feel it would be consistent to return the `Error` enum similar to other set_ and get_ methods. Is this something that can be added to the issue tracker? Also will it break backward compatibility?\r\n\r\nA quick skim through the code tells me the `store` methods may not need that much granularity. It would also break compatibility, indeed. Either way that's outside the scope of this PR.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3001403294/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3001532119","html_url":"https://g